  "title": "Best of Bristol 2015: Festivals",
  "content": "<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-festivals-637x450.jpg\" alt=\"the-fix---festivals\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-10657\" height=\"450\" width=\"637\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-festivals-637x450.jpg 637w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-festivals-300x212.jpg 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-festivals.jpg 682w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 637px) 100vw, 637px\" /></p>\n<p>We run down the best <strong>Festivals</strong> from the last 12-months, and choose our number one.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/unnamed-4.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/unnamed-4-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"unnamed-4\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-10686 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/unnamed-4-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/unnamed-4-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></a>Bristol is surely becoming the bona-fide festival capital of the UK. Barely a Summer weekend goes by without some weird and wonderful event going on. For me, there were two standout festival experiences of the year. Firstly, <b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/love-saves-the-day/\" target=\"_blank\">Love Saves the Day</a></b> built on its burgeoning reputation to flood Eastville Park with glitter and electronics over the May Bank Holiday. Superb sets from some of the world’s best DJs &#8211; Floating Points, Four Tet, Daniel Avery &#8211; were allied with local trumps like Bedmo Disco to produce an atmosphere surprisingly fulsome and upbeat for an inner-city festival.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/033-674x450.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/033-674x450-150x150.jpg\" class=\"alignright wp-image-9615 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/033-674x450-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/033-674x450-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></a>Secondly, <b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/review-arcadias-arachnid-spectacular-lights-up-queen-square-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Arcadia</a></b> brought to Queen’s Square an experience of unparallelled innovation and ambition. Over two nights, the event combined the DJ talents of Roni Size, Annie Mac, Eats Everything and more with pyrotechnics and robotics. I may have been off my cheesebox on goofballs at the time, but having lasers shot directly into my eyes while a giant metal spider loomed over me playing incredible music was absolutely mind-blowing. <strong>(CD)</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/D2DBanner-1024x474.gif\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/D2DBanner-1024x474-150x150.gif\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-8083 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/D2DBanner-1024x474-150x150.gif 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/D2DBanner-1024x474-45x45.gif 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></a>With Love Saves The Day also kicking off on the same afternoon , the 10<sup>th</sup> annual <a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/dot-to-dot-festival-2015/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Dot To Dot</b> <b>Festival </b></a>was the obvious choice for those with a preference for bands over beats, guitars over DJs and a hangover rather than a comedown. Held on gloriously balmy Saturday in late spring, a packed 14 hour programme featured over 125 musical acts playing on 15 stages at 10 venues throughout the city centre. An event so vast that disparity of experience was inevitable, personal highlights included the twisted folk and droll badinage of H Hawkline at The Exchange, a blistering set from ferocious young upstarts Pretty Vicious at Thekla and the garage rock of the excellent PINS at Trinity Centre. <strong>(SH)<br /></strong></p>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"The Fix @ Dot to Dot 2015, Bristol UK\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/O1DF1G6bJ7A?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>\n<hr />\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/thumb.php_-150x150.jpeg\" alt=\"thumb.php\" class=\"alignleft size-thumbnail wp-image-8501\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/thumb.php_-150x150.jpeg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/thumb.php_-45x45.jpeg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" />Recent addition to the cities summer circuit <strong><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/bristol-summer-series1/\" target=\"_blank\">Bristol Summer Series</a></strong> adds a heaveyweight punch to the summers fetivities with it&#8217;s mix of International superstars and up-and-coming alternative acts. Only in it&#8217;s second year it has already established itself as a fim fixture and offers something slightly brasher and fuller than it&#8217;s more indie-focused peers. This year saw George Ezra, Kaiser Chiefs, Seasick Steve, and Jessie J headline, with the likes of Raleigh Ritchie (of unsullied Game Of Thrones fame) and I Am Kloot supporting.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/bristol-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"bristol\" class=\"size-thumbnail wp-image-8789 alignright\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/bristol-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/bristol-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></p>\n<p>To finish I will come at this category from a slightly different angle (I&#8217;m unorthodox, guilty &#8211; get a new rulebook!!) &#8211; <strong><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/review-bristol-comedy-garden-opens-up-with-a-hilarious-heavyweight-punch-to-the-gut/\" target=\"_blank\">Bristol Comedy Garden</a></strong> returned for another year of high jinks in Queens Square.<br />Headlined by comedy legend Stewart Lee, who was his normal acerbic self, the festival saw many of the countries best comedians all give excellent performances for a brilliant week of comedy. <strong>(KM)<br /></strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-green-300x263.png\" alt=\"And the winner is green\" width=\"300\" height=\"263\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-10751 size-medium\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-green-300x263.png 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-green-768x673.png 768w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-green-514x450.png 514w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-green.png 1972w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/image.jpg\" alt=\"image\" width=\"617\" height=\"346\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-10791\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/image.jpg 617w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/image-300x168.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 617px) 100vw, 617px\" /></strong>Still the number one for us, despite the plethora of pretenders to the crown.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Contributions by Kevin McGough (KM), Conal Dougan (CD) and Scott Hammond (SH).</strong></p>\n<p></p>",
